{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Manual, Guide or Instructions?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about manuals, guides and instructions."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Designs a user manual that fulfills both the IT solution needs and the client requirements.   Understand how to write a good user manual."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the operating systems, server operating systems and relevant information related with the user manual."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions within Sentences: How to / Where to / What to + Verb- all of them"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use question words followed by the infinitive of a verb to request specific information."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's a set of directions or steps on how to do something."}, {"type": "example", "content": "So we'll probably get a manual with this computer to tell us what to do before starting it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This pattern is sometimes followed by certain verbs or phrases.<br/>Some of them are:<br/><br/>  <li>Learn</li> <li>Discuss</li> <li>Have information on</li> <li>Know</li> <li>Think about </li> <li>Give an idea of</li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Always use the base form of the verb in this pattern.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">For example:<br/><br/>  <li>Learn how to write.</li> <li>Discuss what to eat.</li> <li>Have information on where to go.</li> <li>Know how to reply.</li> <li>Think about what to choose.</li> <li>Give an idea of what to drink.</li></span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "User manual components"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Although the terms usually overlap, there are certain differences among them."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A guide refers either to a written document, video or booklet."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Generally, manuals and guides include instructions, which refer to processes on assembling or getting something done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Manual</strong>: It refers to a written document which provides information about a product, its maintenance and assistance. It is an official document usually provided by the manufacturer.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Guide</strong>: This is a more generic term and it refers to any type of material which gives information about a product. It might be a video or a booklet. You might find a wide range, from very basic ones to complex and detailed guides.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Instructions</strong>: This is the most generic term of all. It refers to the directions or steps on how to do something. Instructions might be included on a manual or a guide. They can be simple words to describe something.</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "booklet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a book with a few pages"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A guide refers either to a written document, video or booklet. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "further"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "more or additional"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: And if users have further questions?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "maintenance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of keeping something maintained"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A manual usually refers to a formal document which provides information about a product and its maintenance."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "manufacturer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person that makes a product"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In case users want to know additional information. Manufacturers usually include a customer support line to help them solve their questions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "notice"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an announcement or warning"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The most usual elements are the table of contents, a copyright notice."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "representative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person on a phone line that provides support to customers"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Manufacturers usually include a customer support line to help them solve their questions with a representative."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search information about user manuals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you're going to design a user manual, write 5 parts you would include."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the manual to the class"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about manuals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a manual."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I mention 5 parts of the manual."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my manual to the class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jenny</strong>: Hey, I hope this new computer comes with instructions to assemble it. I don&rsquo;t know how to put its parts together.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Ben</strong>: Instructions? Or you mean a manual?</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jenny</strong>: I&rsquo;m not sure. A guide probably? I'm confused about that too. What&rsquo;s the difference?</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Ben</strong>:&nbsp; Well, the terms are usually misused and confused. A manual usually refers to a formal document which provides information about a product and its maintenance. Manufacturers usually hand in an official manual with the product they sell. A guide refers to a written document, video, or booklet. It might contain very detailed information or just generic features of the product. The term guide is sometimes preferred by companies since the word manual sounds a bit too formal.</p>"}, {"time": "52000", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jenny</strong>: So, what about instructions?</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Ben</strong>: They are a bit more generic. Instructions are directions or steps on how to do something. Generally, manuals and guides include instructions which refer to processes in assembling or getting something done.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jenny</strong>: Oh! So, we&rsquo;ll probably get a manual with this computer to tell us what to do before starting it. What shall we find in the manual?</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Ben</strong>: Well, it depends. All manuals can be different; however, there are certain common elements. The most usual elements are the table of contents, a copyright notice, terms and conditions, and graphics and images if necessary. Of course, instructions and procedures are necessary in the body of the manual as it is what users expect to find.</p>"}, {"time": "103000", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jenny</strong>: And if users have further questions?</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Ben</strong>: In case users want to have additional information, manufacturers usually include a customer support line to help them solve their questions with a representative.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jenny</strong>: That was a good explanation. Now, I understand the difference better.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n6le02ob07re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the difference between manuals, guides and instructions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can describe a user manual structure and components."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "In your opinion, is it important to read manuals before using the products? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you thi